# Put a coloured cube into the fixed container (box / plate / bowl) in a single
# call (detect -> pick -> place -> park). PREFERRED whenever the user wants to
# put/drop a cube INTO a box / plate / bowl / container.
# Request: the colour of the cube to pick up, plus optional gripper tightness.
#          The container position is fixed (configured in the skill), so the
#          caller does not supply a destination.
# Response: whether the whole detect -> pick -> place sequence succeeded, plus a
#           human-readable message (with the resolved cube / container position
#           or the failure step).
string color        # required: colour of the cube to pick up and drop in (e.g. "红色" / "red" / "red_cube")
string gripper      # optional: how tightly to close on the cube, 0.0 (open) / 0.5 (standard) / 1.0 (tightest); empty = standard grasp
---
bool ok             # true iff the cube was grasped AND released into the container
string message      # human-readable status: resolved cube, container position, or which step failed
